  "notes": "WRITING:\nThe kanji {曖昧|あいまい} uses rare characters and is often written in hiragana.\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nJapanese communication is often described as {曖昧|あいまい} by non-Japanese speakers. This can be intentional to maintain harmony ({和|わ}) or leave room for interpretation.\n\nUSAGE:\n- {曖昧|あいまい}な{態度|たいど} (ambiguous attitude)\n- {曖昧|あいまい}にする (to make ambiguous, to be evasive)\n- {曖昧|あいまい}さ (ambiguity - noun form)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {曖昧|あいまい}: neutral term for ambiguity\n- うやむや: deliberately obscured\n- あやふや: unreliable or poorly defined",
